I:  To welcome a Chongqing girl into a Yixing family,
I:  I think of a teapot as your family's calling card.
Jushi: Into [b]whose[/b] family?
I:  ...Yours.
Jushi: [b]Into whose family?[/b] Who are you to decide that?
Jushi: Whoever my son ends up with--
Jushi: Even if he stays in America and never comes back,
Jushi: Even if he goes to Beijing, Shanghai, Guangzhou, or Chongqing, 
Jushi: [b]Even if he lives with his wife's family, [/b]
Jushi: [b]He is still my child! [/b]
Jushi: "Into whose family"...(Hou clicks her tongue sharply.)
