title: JushiD2_HeHuanHistory
position: 351,462
---
I: A scholar himself, he often cooperated with artisan siblings to design and commission purple clay teapots,
I: and even inscribed them himself. The teapot became both a medium and an artistic object.
[b]【I hear the call of [u]Courtesan[/u]】[/b]
Jushi: (She bites her lip.) And, what does that have to do with tonight?
I:  Right, right.
<<jump JushiD2_HeHuanStory>>
===


title: JushiD2_HeHuanStory
position: 666,687
---
I: The story goes that while Mansheng was serving as an official in Liyang, 
I: he was responsible for transporting Baiya tribute tea to the capital.
I: The tea arrived on time, the emperor was pleased, 
I: and Mansheng held a banquet for his friends to celebrate.

I: Drums thundered, gongs rang, and firecrackers went off.
I: Delighted, he jumped right in, grabbed two big cymbals, and clashed them open and shut.
I: As the story puts it: "Amid banquet music, he himself took up the great cymbals."
I: That's what inspired him to design the [b][i]Mansheng Sharing-Joy Teapot[/i][/b].
Jushi: (She laughs) A full county magistrate hopping down to clash cymbals himself?
Jushi: Now that's genuine spirit, not bound up by formality.
[b]【I hear myself calling [u]Lv Meng[/u]】[/b]
I: See, here. The upper and lower halves of the pot's body fit together,
(As you speak, you take out two lenticular cards and hand them to Hou.
While she compares and handles them, 
you turn toward the display cabinet, scanning the shelves for the actual teapots.)
I: like two cymbals pressed against each other.
//这里暂停一下沟通页面，空格后重新pull up
<<pause_dialogue>>
(Found it! You put it in front of Hou.)
I: And I think, as a gift tonight, it doesn't have to mean just marital harmony.
I: Friends, relatives, even people who hardly know one another...
I: Getting to sit down at the same table is a good thing in itself.
I: As a gift, it carries both a wish for success in one's career and the joy of gathering together.
I: Plus, its name is self-evident, making its meanings not too obscure.
Jushi: Quite. Different minds, different sides.
Jushi: You have to sit down at the same table first before you can even talk about harmony.
(She presses her lips together.)
Jushi: That's a good story behind it.
<<jump JushiD2_HeHuanConfirm>>
===

