title: JushiD2_Delivery
position: 265,2037
---
You quietly finish up what you're doing.
(The Lay Buddhist slowly turns toward the window.
The sun is beginning to set. There are fewer people on Gunan Street now.
Some push their bicycles; others start their electric scooters with a couple of little chirps.
Here and there, a beetle-like car pulls away.
Your gaze moves from the backlit window frame to her.
She is thin, with very short hair, alert and spirited.
The skin on her face clings tightly to her bones, yet her cheeks are not hollow.
Dim orange sunlight catches her cheekbones, neck, and pronounced wrist bones.
After all that commotion, no one has switched on the shop lights. 
Beyond the glow around her, everything looks dark and cold.
She seems warmly dressed, though.
a coral pink cashmere twinset, its pills carefully trimmed, with slightly worn plastic buttons in the same shade.
She smiles very gently.)
//这里暂停一下沟通页面，空格后重新pull up
<<pause_dialogue>>
I: It's all wrapped. I'll send it over at six.
Jushi: Not [b]sent out[/b] at 18:00—[b]delivered[/b] by 18:00.
Jushi: About thirty minutes into dinner. Room 1314 at the Kempinski.
Jushi: I'll head out first. Ring it out on your end.
Jushi: I'll transfer the money straight to Shao Wei.
Jushi: Young lady, what's your name?
I: My surname is Wang. 
Jushi: Wang. Thank you for all your trouble.
(I watch her walk down the lane. There's nothing else to do today. 
What vehicle will she take to leave Gunan Street?
Her figure turns right at the end of the lane and disappears.)
<<hide_character "jushi">>
<<jump JushiD2_Teacher>>
===

title: JushiD2_Teacher
position: 265,2262
---
<<wait 0.4>>
<<play_sfx "doorbell">>
<<wait 0.8>>
<<show_character "teacher">>
<<wait 0.3>>
Master Shao:  (She pushes the door open, speaking on speakerphone.)
(She drops a bag onto the table, gestures toward you with her chin, and covers the receiver.)
Master Shao: I brought these from [i]Huanglong Mountain[/i] for you this week. Everything all right?
(Before you can answer, she goes back to the phone.)
Master Shao: Oh, sis! What brings you here today?
Master Shao: All good, all good. Mm-hmm.
Master Shao: This girl here? She [b]is[/b] capable, you know.
Master Shao: Hurry home? Oh! Take care! Yes, yes. Bye now. 
(She hangs up and turns to you.)
//这里暂停一下沟通页面，空格后重新pull up
<<pause_dialogue>>
(It's the same tall, impeccably dressed Master Shao.)
//这里暂停一下沟通页面，空格后重新pull up
<<pause_dialogue>>
Master Shao: You have no idea what her life used to be like.
Master Shao: Used to live [b]such[/b] a comfy life!
Master Shao: Her father-in-law was this in the county government. (She gives a thumbs-up.) 
Master Shao: Oh, those were the days! 
Master Shao: All that investment coming in, the connections they had!
Master Shao: She married into quite the family. Lived very well.
Master Shao: Her sister-in-law was even her best friend from high school. The whole family doted on her little boy.
Master Shao: She wasn't like this back then. 
Master Shao: Looked down her nose at everyone, always boasting about her husband's family.
Master Shao: She and her husband had easy jobs, kept their salaries for themselves, and lived and ate at home. 
Master Shao: Oh, the things they spent money on!
Master Shao: And then somebody reported her. 
Master Shao: Some people just can't bear to see others doing well, can they? 
Master Shao: Such a pity. She had a promising career ahead of her.
Master Shao: They found problems in the accounts at her father's company, too.
Master Shao: Ah, if they'd only held on a few more years, the whole company might have been theirs. 
Master Shao: Why the hurry?
Master Shao: One must know when to hold back. A little discretion goes a long way.
[b]【I hear the call of [u]Ke Xiang[/u], while hearing myself calling [u]Ke Xiang[/u]】[/b]
Master Shao: Such is fate!
Master Shao: Even her father-in-law was investigated.
Master Shao: Nothing came of it in the end, but how could they go on living under the same roof?
Master Shao: And right at that moment, her husband moved out. Only later did they find out...
I: He ran off with the money?
Master Shao: That drunken, chain-smoking fool!
Master Shao: Him? As if he could pull that off! He had another woman!
Master Shao: That man had been spoiled rotten since childhood. 
Master Shao: He kicked up a fuss until he got his divorce and married someone else.
Master Shao: Her own family couldn't help her. Miserable, really.
Master Shao: In the first lunar month of 2008,
Master Shao: she finally moved out for good. She deliberately waited until her son had fallen asleep.
Master Shao: They loaded the last box of her personal things into the car.
Master Shao: The engine started, the headlights came on,
Master Shao: and there was the little boy, standing at the courtyard gate.
Master Shao: Crying in his grandmother's arms, calling out for his mother.
Master Shao: His grandmother couldn't possibly let him go running after her. 
Master Shao: Imagine what his father would do.
Master Shao: Both of them crying. Mother and son.
Master Shao: Oh...
Master Shao: I've heard her tell that story more times than I can count.
Master Shao: The house, the son—what could she take with her?
Master Shao: And you haven't seen that new wife of his!
Master Shao: She used to work under Hou Li. Who knows how often Hou looked down her nose at her.
Master Shao: (Tsk.) What a miserable business.
-> Master, aren't you her friend?
    <<jump JushiD2_TeacherFriend>>
-> Couldn't she have refused to divorce him?
    <<jump JushiD2_TeacherDivorce>>
===

title: JushiD2_TeacherFriend
position: 512,2487
---
Master Shao: Of course. Why would I ask you to look after her if we weren't friends?
I: ...Oh... nothing.
Master Shao: Huh? What have I said against her?
(She glances down at her phone.)
Master Shao: Yixing is only this big. Everyone knows everybody's family business.
Master Shao: It's hardly a secret.
<<jump JushiD2_Order>>
===

title: JushiD2_TeacherDivorce
position: 232,2487
---
(She pauses.)
Master Shao: Ah. What happens between husband and wife is never something you can explain in a sentence or two.
Master Shao: Marriage, eh!
Master Shao: She's been through enough over the years.
Master Shao: A woman starting over doesn't need every old story dragged out again.
I: ……
Master Shao: Look, she practices meditation, does good deeds, and leads a quiet life now.
Master Shao: What's wrong with that?
<<jump JushiD2_Order>>
